 "brief_summary": "A Randomized, Double-blind, Parallel-group Study to Evaluate the Effect of Bydureon Compared with Placebo on 24-hour Glucose Control in Metformin-treated Patients with Type 2 Diabetes.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) treated with stable dose of metformin \\> or = to 1500mg/day as monotherapy for at least 8 weeks\n* Hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) 7% to 10% at screening\n* Body mass index (BMI) \\< or = to 45 kg/m2\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* History of taking antihyperglycemic therapy other than metformin or metformin extended release (XR) during the 8 weeks prior to screening\n* History of taking a dipeptidyl peptidase-4 (DPP-4) inhibitor or pramlintide during 12 weeks prior to screening\n* History of potent, inhaled or intrapulmonary steroids 3 months prior to screening or during the study\n* History of prescription or over the counter weight loss medication during 3 months prior to screening\n* Previous exposure to exenatide or any glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonist during 6 months prior to screening",
  "sex": "ALL",
  "minimum_age": "18 Years",
  "maximum_age": "75 Years",
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
  "std_ages": [
   "ADULT",
   "OLDER_ADULT"
  ]
 },
